# playpick gave mode=battleground map=conquest spec=druid:restoration
# style=auto view=1280x800 save=fresh. 1280x800 is desktop, not touch, so
# isTouchMode() gates the AUTO toggle off and playbot's own play() should fall
# back to `good` (the "no-autocast-toggle" note in scripts/playbot.ts) --
# meaning this cell resolves, in practice, to the good-style restoration-druid
# battleground pull that direction.md's [[#7]] line has been asking for since
# 2026-09-26: the only prior healer/battleground pull (flags, druid:
# restoration, genuine touch AUTO) found a healer that casts but never steers,
# and stood still until it died, and the line's own next step was "worth a
# good-style restoration druid on the same map before concluding anything
# about the class rather than the driver's own positioning gap." This is also
# conquest's first healer-role pull (prior conquest sessions were
# priest:shadow flee, druid:balance good, and a bare-idle control -- all dps).
open
targets
shot front

tap battleground
tap map:conquest
targets
shot conquest-picked

tap class:druid:restoration
tap pull
waitscreen fight 15
shot pulled
state
targets

play auto 60
shot mid1
state
bill
says

wait 5
play auto 60
shot mid2
state
bill

wait 5
play auto 90
shot mid3
state
bill
says
targets
